<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       PYRELANDS_DEDICATED_GRAZER_1 — how a burrower gets to decide.

       Same supported modder hook the fire-hawk and furnace-beast use, and
       for the same reasons: Core's Defs/ThinkTreeDefs/Animal.xml carries
       <li Class="ThinkNode_SubtreesByTag"><insertTag>Animal_PreWander</insertTag></li>,
       and a ThinkTreeDef declaring that insertTag is spliced in there. No
       MayRequire: Animal_PreWander is Core.

       🔑 UNLIKE the fire-hawk/furnace-beast trees, this one carries NO
       species gate at the C# level either — RM_JobGiver_BurrowOnFire's own
       null-modExtension check IS the gate (RM_BurrowOnFireExtension, opt-in
       per race), the same shape CreatureBehaviors' RM_ThinkTree_ShadowFollow
       already uses for the shade-follow mechanism. That is deliberate: a
       second dedicated burrower the biome wants later needs only the
       extension in its own ThingDef, no new ThinkTreeDef and no new C#.

       insertPriority 56: just above the fire-hawk's 55 and the furnace-
       beast's 54 — going to ground ahead of the fire is safety-critical for
       whatever species carries the extension, so it should preempt an
       igniter's own opportunistic behaviour rather than contend with it for
       a number. In practice the three never compete for the same pawn: each
       gate (comp, comp, modExtension) is species-exclusive.
  ======================================================================== -->
  <ThinkTreeDef>
    <defName>RM_BurrowOnFire</defName>
    <insertTag>Animal_PreWander</insertTag>
    <insertPriority>56</insertPriority>
    <thinkRoot Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.Pyrelands.RM_JobGiver_BurrowOnFire" />
      </subNodes>
    </thinkRoot>
  </ThinkTreeDef>

</Defs>
